diff_hunk:
@@ -2,14 +2,15 @@
   description = "Bundle Nix derivations into AppImages";

   inputs = {
-    nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable";
+    logos-nix.url = "github:logos-co/logos-nix";
+    nixpkgs.follows = "logos-nix/nixpkgs";
     nix-bundle-dir = {
       url = "github:logos-co/nix-bundle-dir";
       inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";

body:
`nix-bundle-dir` now brings in its own `logos-nix` input (see flake.lock), which isn’t being overridden here. This causes duplicate `logos-nix`/`nixpkgs` instances and can lead to inconsistent package sets and larger closures. Consider adding `inputs.logos-nix.follows = "logos-nix";` under the `nix-bundle-dir` input (or otherwise wiring it to the same `logos-nix`/`nixpkgs`), then regenerate `flake.lock`.
```suggestion
      inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";
      inputs.logos-nix.follows = "logos-nix";
```
